A||||3||Fearless Freep||Heat Coated "Y" Pipe Question||||1||
Z||000000||Fearless Freep||10-02-2000||07:49 PM||||If you had your y pipe heat coated inside and out, would you still need the heatshields installed??  Or would you bake something??  EGR Tube.....Coil.....||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||10-02-2000||08:22 PM||||Probably not since coatings lower under hood temperatures by as much as 40 degrees. It would still be a good idea to have them on because the lower your underhood temperatures are the longer your accessories will last. I have my crossover pipe coated but I am still going to install the heat shields.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-02-2000||08:48 PM||||I'd install them just for safety. I'm not sure just which ones and where you mean. You want to deflect all the heat you can away from the ignition parts and intake. The cooler those are the happier they will be.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-03-2000||09:36 AM||||my ceramic wrapped manifolds kept the engine bay cooler than the heat coated headers did. i'd put the heat shields on... and wrap it all up with 1/8" ceramic header wrap... <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>   thromo-tec header wrap.. about $40. ||||reg||1
